course: dictionary
lesson: 13256
title: Gleaming: shining words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Gleaming is a describing word. It paints a picture of something shiny because it is clean, polished or wet, so the light bounces off it. «Dad polished his gleaming shoes before the wedding.» The shoes shine because they are clean and polished.
explain: Gleam can also be a verb, which means to give out or reflect a soft, bright light. «The river gleamed in the sun.» Here gleamed is the action: the water is shining. Gleaming is the -ing form, so it can describe a thing, like a gleaming river.
explain: Writers use gleaming to help you see a scene. In The Wind in the Willows, Toad's new motor-car is gleaming and splendid. Eyes can gleam too: «Her eyes were gleaming with a sly plan.» Then the word shows a feeling, such as excitement or a secret idea, not just light.
fact: Gleaming means shining brightly because something is clean, polished or wet.
fact: «Gleaming» can describe shoes, cars, teeth or wet roads.
fact: Gleam as a verb means to give out or reflect a soft, bright light.
fact: «The river gleams in the sun» shows light shining on water.
fact: Words like «gleaming» help readers picture a scene in their minds.
exercise: «The gleaming car was parked outside the school.» What does gleaming mean here? | Covered in mud and dust | Very small and quiet | *Shining brightly because it is clean and polished | Broken into pieces
exercise: «The moon's light gleamed on the lake.» Find and copy the verb. | *gleamed | lake | moon | light
exercise: «Her eyes were gleaming with a sly plan.» What might gleaming show here? | Feeling cold | Tiredness after a long day | *Excitement or a secret idea | Being hungry
test: «The gleaming teeth made the toothpaste advert look fun.» What does gleaming mean? | *Shining brightly because clean | Cold to touch | Hidden under a blanket | Ugly and dirty
test: Choose the word that means shining and polished. | *gleaming | dull | muddy | faded
exam: Mia says «gleaming» means dull. Which answer is right? | *No, it means shining brightly because clean, polished or wet | Yes, it means dark and hidden | No, it means very loud | Yes, it means dull and grey
